Z||000000||DrRodey||10-22-2000||01:20 PM||||I know this has nothing to do with my Fieros and i'm sorry but i can't get any reliable info anywhere else so please bear with me.... Ok heres the scoop, I recently found a schmuck who sold me a Ford 302 v-8 for $25 and i need to know.... Will it or will it not bolt on to an AX-5 transmission like what is in my Wrangler or do i need to find a ford tranny somewhere cheap.... Secondly, What else will i need to change when doing the swap.  <P>I know this is a little out of the range of the forum but it is the best place i know to get answers and no one i've talked to, including the off-road shops in the area, will give me a strait answer.  Thanks for any help.<P>------------------<BR>'88 Formula CONVERTABLE<BR>'85 Coupe<BR> <IMG SRC="http://freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/files/smallfc.JPG"> <BR> <A HREF="http://freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/HomePlace.html" TARGET=_blank>freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/HomePlace.html</A> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Seanh||10-22-2000||01:36 PM||||As far as I know, I dont think it will bolt up like that. Sorry I cant help more, but Im not to knowledgeabout in field like this. Also, is there something wrong with the engine you want to change out, or just to get more power? I would be a little affraid to put a $25 engine in if nothing if wrong with the old one. I would check it over real good before hand. If nothing is really wrong with it, then you got a great deal.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System<p>[This message has been edited by Seanh (edited 10-22-2000).]||||reg||1
